{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545858-having-a-hard-time-with-this-awakening-i-m-plotting-out","id":1545858,"title":"Having a hard time with this awakening I'm plotting out","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-14T10:16:06-08:00","id":1545858,"title":"Having a hard time with this awakening I'm plotting out","content":"So last time I ran mage we ended with a NPC beginning his mystery play, as the watchtower drew in the Mastigos. The NPC is magically compelled to obsess over a magical item, but the Mastigos hid the memory with Mind veiling. This did not stop the magical compulsion to obsess, but without anything to focus on it's been driving him crazy. Instead of breaking though Stygia called out to him, and he'll have to attempt to complete his mystery play and discover this memory that was taken, or sacrifice.<br /> <br /> The Mastigos is taking on the role within the Mystery Play as the &quot;Occulter&quot; the shade that hides the Truth from others, but honestly I'm not really sure what to actually have him do that isn't just <i>watching </i>an NPC so their thing. Any ideas?<br /> <br /> I'm not worried about the rest of the cabal, I have something in mind for those outside the awakening that will keep them involved and busy, it's just this Mastigos issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T12:10:02-08:00","id":1545866,"title":"","content":"For the moment we'll set aside the fact that as a Mastigos being in a Stygian Mystery Play is an odd situation to be in (joining an Adyton requires a mage to be of the appropriate Path and exceptionally succeed at Revealing the Mystery of the Lucid), since that sounds like it's either a done deal or else would necessitate changing the Prospect's Watchtower before the next session; unless he gains and tries to use Mana the only practical difference is in knowing how the NPC is seeing the world.<br /> <br /> In the context of being part of the Mystery Play, worry less about &quot;having the player do things&quot; and more about directing the Adyton's narrative toward him in ways appropriate to the Prospect's tests, likely in the context of what he's done to their memory \u2014 if they pass the trials, both the memory modification and the compulsion will be cleared away, and the trials continue until they either spend the Experiences to get their first dot of Gnosis or conclusively fail one of the tests (tests which have no obligation to keep intruders safe).<br /> <br /> The Prospect could try to bargain for their memory back, or try to extract an explanation for why the Mastigos hid it from them, and the magical item in question is almost certainly going to be important regardless. Basically just run the chapter as normal with the added weight of mythic symbolism on the Mastigos and the NPC's perspectives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T13:35:32-08:00","id":1545874,"title":"","content":"As Satchel said, usually only other Moros can be pulled into a Moros Awakening. However, your Mastigos was already heavily involved in that NPC's occult development, so he could be &quot;incorporated&quot; as a result of that. It's a unique Mystery the PC can boast about later on, especially among Mages that study Awakenings (Alethians).<br /> <br /> Now, the most common lesson of Stygia is learning to let go, and the NPC has a number of things that count:<br /> \u2022 The Obsession towards the magic item.<br /> \u2022 Interest in the supernatural, in general.<br /> \u2022 The Veling spell that protects him.<br /> \u2022 Having the Mastigos as a protector.<br /> \u2022 Whatever would anchor him to his mundane life.<br /> <br /> Your player's actions may steer that NPCs choices. Depending on what happens, the NPC may:<br /> \u2022 Fully pass the trial and Awaken.<br /> \u2022 Receive a Supernal right to claim the magic item.<br /> \u2022 Be forever Supernally separated from the item.<br /> \u2022 Be forever Supernally separated from the Mastigos.<br /> \u2022 Lose a major personal attachment from his Sleeper life.<br /> \u2022 Let go of the supernatural, but become a Sleepwalker.<br /> \u2022 Let go of the supernatural, but become a Banisher.<br /> <br /> Just about the only way to fail that trial is to try and keep things as they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T14:16:38-08:00","id":1545881,"title":"","content":"Hm, I don't see anything that says the Watchtowers can't pull in a mage from any path if they are important to the Adyton, but either way it doesn't matter, the Mastigos is part of this.<br /> <br /> You did give me an interesting idea of having the spell and the memory it is hiding seek out the Mastigos to keep it hidden from the NPC, and have the NPC pursuing the memory and have to decide if he wants it back or not. The magic item may even get pulled away from where it's been hidden and placed somewhere nearby the NPCs path. <br /> <br /> Hm, lots of symbolism to think of, tyvm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T14:31:02-08:00","id":1545884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545858-having-a-hard-time-with-this-awakening-i-m-plotting-out?p=1545881#post1545881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I don't see anything that says the Watchtowers can't pull in a mage from any path if they are important to the Adyton</div> </div> </div> </div>For reference:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of Sorcery p131, &quot;Detection&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The presence of a Lucid \u2014 no matter which form of Awakening he\u2019s in \u2014 triggers the Peripheral Mage Sight of all mages within range of their own senses. Active Mage Sight of any Path or Arcanum reveals the Pneuma within the Lucid\u2019s Patten as a shimmering, golden light. For the four Paths that do not share a Watchtower with the Awakening in progress, that\u2019s as much as they can observe. Mages who did once sign the Watchtower creating the Lustrum, however, have a better view.<br /> <br /> Mages of the correct Path that use Active Mage Sight on the Lucid still don\u2019t see the symbolic landscape she\u2019s encountering, but instead a coruscating aura around her, which spreads to anything she\u2019s particularly engaging with as part of her Awakening.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Signs of Sorcery p132, &quot;Entering the Adyton&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Synching up to an Adyton to intrude into it requires Mage Sight of the correct Path and both Ruling Arcana, and an exceptional success on an attempt to Reveal a Lucid character undergoing a Waking World Dream Awakening. For purposes of Mage Sight, an Awakening is an Opacity 6 Mystery.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T14:49:32-08:00","id":1545885,"title":"","content":"Right but that's specifically for <i>invading</i> an Adyton, not being picked to be part of it by the watchtower","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T15:32:25-08:00","id":1545887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545858-having-a-hard-time-with-this-awakening-i-m-plotting-out?p=1545885#post1545885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right but that's specifically for <i>invading</i> an Adyton, not being picked to be part of it by the watchtower</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is a thing that is largely unprecedented within the text except in basic terms like your likeness being used for symbolic purposes to convey something to the Prospect or the Prospect being directed to you by the symbolism of their journey, neither of which shows you the symbolic landscape they're seeing. I share the mechanics for entering an Adyton because that's the closest thing to what you're describing that exists in the books besides the theoretical capacity for a different Watchtower-related Lustrum shenanigan that happens to involve casting another mage in an ongoing Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T15:45:17-08:00","id":1545888,"title":"","content":"Right, so I'll use those mechanics if the Moros player decides he wants to have a look inside, but it isn't what is going on with the Mastigos so I don't see the relevance.<br /> <br /> The Mastigos has been given a role to fulfill and can see what the NPC can see because the watchtower said &quot;you're a part of thi,&quot; regardless of the desire of the Mastigos either way. That's what I'm here for, which you already offered aid for","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T18:11:38-08:00","id":1545899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545858-having-a-hard-time-with-this-awakening-i-m-plotting-out?p=1545888#post1545888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, so I'll use those mechanics if the Moros player decides he wants to have a look inside, but it isn't what is going on with the Mastigos so I don't see the relevance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The relevance is that as far as precedent from the books goes, the situation you were asking about doesn't happen. That's it.<br /> <br /> The circumstance that you have created is firmly in the realm of plot device \u2014 the <i>only</i> support for it is that it's not explicitly stated to be impossible in the text because the text does not describe the Watchtowers independently drawing in mages who've already Awakened in the first place.<br /> <br /> That's why I prefaced my initial advice with setting aside the fact that getting involved perceptually in a Mystery Play set in a given Supernal Realm requires a signature on that Realm's Watchtower, because you've already described it as happening, playing the ball as it lies is common practice in TTRPGs, and it seems having the Prospect's crisis open the door to Pandemonium instead is off the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T18:58:42-08:00","id":1545903,"title":"","content":"Right the book says some things about awakenings, and then nothing about what I'm doing, so why cite parts of the book that don't have to do with this, that's what I'm confused about but I don't really feel like this matters and we'll just keep going in circles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T19:51:38-08:00","id":1545909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545858-having-a-hard-time-with-this-awakening-i-m-plotting-out?p=1545903#post1545903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right the book says some things about awakenings, and then nothing about what I'm doing, so why cite parts of the book that don't have to do with this</div> </div> </div> </div>Because this doesn't exist in the books and you are asking a question about how to handle something in a game that has books on the forums for that game. The closest thing in the books to what you are describing is entering an Adyton, which can explicitly happen by accident and casts the intruder in the Mystery Play while they're within range of the Prospect's senses.<br /> <br /> There is no real next-closest thing described in the books to &quot;the Watchtower picking an outside character to be a participant in the Adyton,&quot; because the Watchtowers are historically specific contrasts to the Exarchs in their degree of direct meddling in the world \u2014 the full spectrum of technical possibility behind undetailed things like the powers of Sacred Artifacts or weird slants on Imperial spells to directly Awaken people nevertheless runs into the fact that the Watchtowers themselves are not under the control of anybody and do not evidence any clear agenda besides offering the Awakening to Prospects who meet the necessary criteria.<br /> <br /> We have systems for joining in on an Awakening and it was more expedient to state up front that this is unusual when those are the only context we have for doing so and then offer advice as it would pertain to the normal situation. You voiced doubts about there being anything limiting the Path of a mage subjected to a process that is not described anywhere in the books when given that up-front statement and were then given a citation of the text describing how the closest thing to what you described is limited by Path.<br /> <br /> I began my actual advice with the note that the Adyton is a filter centered on the Lucid mage-to-be because the systems we have for being involved with an Adyton at the level where you can see the symbolism the Prospect sees has potential consequences and rewards beyond simply knowing they're in the middle of an Awakening. Pushing back and drawing an arbitrary line between the established systems for joining an Adyton and this situation makes it unclear if any of those consequences are actually on the table anymore or if this is just being used as a more involved way of watching an Awakening from the outside with no added risk of metamorphosis, opportunity to harvest Pneuma, or risk to Wisdom.<br /> <br /> I cannot devil's-proof what you've described as impossible any more than I can prove my real-life house <i>isn'</i>t haunted by real-life imperceptible spirits. The narrative <i>fait accompli</i> of a Mastigos being in a Stygian Mystery Play in your game has been established regardless, which means the most I can do for your game absent the willingness and/or ability to rewrite events into a more plausible form is to emphasize that the situation you have created is a weird one that is breaking with known rules and established precedents, possibly due to additional tampering with the Watchtower by a third party, which potentially brings Supernal attention and Aponoia into play.<br /> <br /> You mentioned having things to keep the rest of the cabal busy while the Mastigos deals with this entanglement. Are they elsewhere? Also, given the discussion it's probably worth clarifying: is this Mystery Play a Waking World Dream or has the Mastigos been pulled along on a Supernal Journey in a further break from conventional understanding?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T20:22:50-08:00","id":1545911,"title":"","content":"I did not ask if it was possible for a Mastigos to force his way into a Stygian awakening, I asked how can I involve a PC in an NPCs awakening in a way that is more than just a passive observer, which you answered in a helpful way, thank you for that.<br /> <br /> Everything after that has been citations to rules about things that <i>are not happening </i>in my game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T21:07:27-08:00","id":1545912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545858-having-a-hard-time-with-this-awakening-i-m-plotting-out?p=1545911#post1545911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything after that has been citations to rules about things that <i>are not happening </i>in my game</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you've made that abundantly clear.<br /> <br /> You've also continued to express confusion about why anyone would bring up <i>the only published thing remotely close to the thing you've described as happening in your game</i> which, as Teatime said, underlines the thing that is happening in your game as a unique occurrence.<br /> <br /> If you have your own system figured out for this thing that is arbitrarily different from getting into an Adyton by Revelation, that's fine, but that's information you didn't see fit to provide and it's upsetting to be repeatedly told that it is somehow hard to understand why it would be relevant for someone to bring up the only point of reference anybody outside your troupe would have for mages getting entangled with other characters' Awakenings in support of the statement that being part of another mage's Awakening typically means you're on the Path they're seeking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T07:32:12-08:00","id":1545932,"title":"","content":"What's upsetting to me is that I've made it abundantly clear that it isn't relevant and why and you keep insisting it is. I've also explained how it happened, I did so in my very first comment in response to you and Teatime, so I'm not sure what &quot;that's information you didn't see fit to provide&quot; would mean. <br /> <br /> I've said already that we are just going in circles and I continue to be correct in that, please, don't try to convince me about what is and is not relevant to my game anymore. If you have anything else to add to the actual question I presented in this post, I'd be happy to hear it, you gave useful insights there that I appreciate, otherwise, we're just wasting our time going back and forth on this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T08:02:28-08:00","id":1545939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1545858-having-a-hard-time-with-this-awakening-i-m-plotting-out?p=1545932#post1545932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's upsetting to me is that I've made it abundantly clear that it isn't relevant and why and you keep insisting it is. I've also explained how it happened, I did so in my very first comment in response to you and Teatime, so I'm not sure what &quot;that's information you didn't see fit to provide&quot; would mean.<br /> <br /> I've said already that we are just going in circles and I continue to be correct in that, please, don't try to convince me about what is and is not relevant to my game anymore. If you have anything else to add to the actual question I presented in this post, I'd be happy to hear it, you gave useful insights there that I appreciate, otherwise, we're just wasting our time going back and forth on this</div> </div> </div> </div>My final point of clarification, then:<br /> <br /> The relevance I am referring to is the context of my second reply, elaborating on your confusion as to why my first reply \u2014 supported by Teatime's reply \u2014 quoted the thing from the books that I mistook as the situation you described due to the ambiguity of the language you used in the original post \u2014 given that the situation is still a PC being involved with an NPC's Awakening, &quot;Stygia called out to [the Prospect]&quot; and &quot;the Watchtower drew in the Mastigos&quot; are sufficiently broad that I made what I would consider the reasonable initial assumption that you were referring to joining an Adyton in the normal context with the unusual involvement of a mage from a different Path, rather than a novel phenomenon that can ignore the stated limitations of inadvertently joining an Adyton through Mage Sight, because the original post did not give any reason to think otherwise at the time.<br /> <br /> You have since clarified that the situation you described was not the one that I and others had mistaken it for. I have been trying to explain the initial confusion, which no amount of later clarification can undo without a time machine. I am sorry that you received the mistaken impression that I have been telling you what is relevant to your game instead of what is relevant to my attempt to explain why I mentioned something that confused you due to a gap in information. Hopefully this qualifies as breaking the circle.<br /> <br /> <br /> On the topic of the actual question in the post, I <i>did</i> ask further clarifying questions that haven't been answered, chief among them being whether this Awakening is a Waking World Dream or a Supernal Journey. Is the Mastigos still participating in the real world in parallel with the Awakening or is he in a position to meet with Shades not overlaid on Phenomenal actors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-15T10:22:43-08:00","id":1545954,"title":"","content":"It's a waking world dream. Based on the advice you guys gave I have decided to start the Mystery Play out in a prison of brass to represent the magic item he is obsessed with (and the fact that the awakening started in the sanctum where they hid the item). He'll have to confront his a Patriarch, the Occulter, the Memory, and the magic item before he can awaken, so I'll give the Mastigos opportunities to fuck things up or not throughout that. <br /> <br /> The Mastigos can sorta kinda see the phenomenal world, it's just hard through the magic of the watchtower and can <i>try</i> to interact with it. <br /> <br /> The rest of the cabal will be dealing with a Moros Banisher (ideological) that senses the start of the Awakening and is in his way to inturupt it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}